Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Kazuhiro Ohnishi
Title: Lifetime Employment and Mixed Cournot Duopoly with State-Owned and Joint-Stock Firms
Abstract: This paper examines a mixed duopoly model in which a state-owned firm competes with a joint-stock firm. The following two stages are considered. In the first stage, each firm can simultaneously and independently decide whether or not to offer lifetime employment as a strategic commitment. In the second stage, each firm simultaneously and independently chooses its actual output. The paper shows that there are two equilibrium solutions in the model.
Keywords: Joint-stock firm,lifetime employment,mixed duopoly,state-owned firm
Journal: International Journal of Management, Accounting and Economics
Pages: 1-9
Volume: 5
Issue: 1
Year: 2018
DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.17540618
